  "id": "COMPOUND:25576 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between [(1R,2S,4R,6R,9R,10S,11R,12S,14R,15R,18R)-14-Acetyloxy-6-(furan-3-yl)-10-(2-methoxy-2-oxoethyl)-7,9,11,15-tetramethyl-3,17-dioxapentacyclo[9.6.1.02,9.04,8.015,18]octadec-7-en-12-yl] (E)-2-methylbut-2-enoate and BT-474, through a multi-tiered mechanism involving protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This compound appears to target Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn is targeted by Anolobine and another related compound. These targets are implicated in the regulation of cellular signaling pathways, and their interaction with BT-474 suggests a possible role in modulating cellular processes in the tumor cell line. The evidence is supported by a chain of targets that connects the compound to BT-474, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of protein-tyrosine phosphatase suggest a potential role in signaling pathways that are dysregulated in BT-474, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the therapeutic relevance.",
